      "problem": "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )((5-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +9) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
